select b.id,79,null,$q$In a dry test tube, 2 mL of HCl (0.1 N) is taken. To this, 4 mL of NaOH (0.1 N) is added. The solution is stirred well, followed by the addition of 2 drops of phenolphthalein. What will be the colour of the solution?$q$,$q$Colourless$q$,$q$Red$q$,$q$Pink$q$,$q$Blue$q$,0.98,'{}'::text[],$q$NDA_II_2026_GK_079$q$,$q$In a dry test tube, 2 mL of HCl (0.1 N) is taken. To this, 4 mL of NaOH (0.1 N) is added. The solution is stirred well, followed by the addition of 2 drops of phenolphthalein. What will be the colour of the solution?$q$,$q$Colourless$q$,$q$Red$q$,$q$Pink$q$,$q$Blue$q$,$q$345e2908447f2f2326c3ae9b6d42f3405d79ecb3152a4f1208fd3aac844adaa9$q$,$q$C$q$,'MODEL_ONLY',$q$dp-solved://NDA_2026_II_GAT_GK_SET_A$q$,null,$q$C$q$,$q$C$q$,false,$q$Science & Technology$q$,$q$Chemistry$q$,$q$Acids, Bases, pH & Commercial Inorganic Salts$q$,$q$Neutralisation and indicator colour$q$,'Knowledge',$q$Single MCQ$q$,$q$PATTERN.DIRECT$q$,$q$Step 1: HCl gives $2\times0.1=0.2$ meq; NaOH gives $4\times0.1=0.4$ meq.
