select b.id,87,null,$q$Consider the following statements regarding hydrogen bonds:
I. Hydrogen bonds can only form when hydrogen is bonded to oxygen, nitrogen or fluorine.
II. Hydrogen bonds are intramolecular only.
III. The strength of a hydrogen bond decreases with a decrease in the electronegativity of the two bonded atoms.
Which of the statements given above is/are not correct?$q$,$q$I only$q$,$q$II only$q$,$q$I and II$q$,$q$II and III$q$,0.98,'{}'::text[],$q$NDA_II_2026_GK_087$q$,$q$Consider the following statements regarding hydrogen bonds:
I. Hydrogen bonds can only form when hydrogen is bonded to oxygen, nitrogen or fluorine.
II. Hydrogen bonds are intramolecular only.
III. The strength of a hydrogen bond decreases with a decrease in the electronegativity of the two bonded atoms.
Which of the statements given above is/are not correct?$q$,$q$I only$q$,$q$II only$q$,$q$I and II$q$,$q$II and III$q$,$q$cb8e8b44da15ddc51c0f9d263fc28117770a0e9bd526ebaf496900941572b767$q$,$q$B$q$,'MODEL_ONLY',$q$dp-solved://NDA_2026_II_GAT_GK_SET_A$q$,null,$q$B$q$,$q$B$q$,false,$q$Science & Technology$q$,$q$Chemistry$q$,$q$Chemical Bonding & Molecular Structure$q$,$q$Hydrogen bonding$q$,'Knowledge',$q$3-Statement Combination$q$,$q$PATTERN.STATEMENT.3$q$,$q$I is the standard textbook condition (H bonded to N, O or F), so it is taken as correct.
II is wrong: hydrogen bonds are both intermolecular and intramolecular.
III is correct: lower electronegativity gives a weaker bond.
Only II is not correct.
